  "query_preview": "..\nAnother round of little to no rainfall is expected tonight, \nespecially for the CNMI, as the current wedge of drier air lifts \nnorth. Then, Precipitable Water (PWAT) values of at least 2.0 inches\npaired with light and variable winds will move over the region, so \nscattered island-effect showers in the afternoon are expected for \nGuam over the next couple of days. Next week, light to gentle trade \nwinds will return to the region, so afternoon island-effect showers \nwill be concentrated over the western shorelines and adjacent coastal\nwaters for Guam. Shower coverage will remain isolated for the CNMI \nthroughout the forecast period.",
